@talks pell
// TW1, the Talk a while pack: Pell Okafor's own talks. Easygoing, chatty; "Oi oi", "Right, so"; stories that go
// sideways; teases fondly about sleep and food. Mum's shop from tier friend only; not the opened messages (beat pell.6).

== screw-tin
topic: hobby
them: Right, so. This tin. Screws from seven ships. One from every ship I've fixed something on.
them: This one's from a ferry. I fixed a kettle. On a ferry. Long story. Bit long.   #funny
ask: Do you keep anything like that? A little collection?
listen: Which screw's your favourite?
  them: The bent one. Holds the whole tin together, morally.   #funny
share: Not yet. I might start one.
  them: Do! I'll give you your first. A Wren one. Then you're official.   #warm
cheer: I collect naps. Like you.
  them: Oi oi! Slander. Accurate, but slander.   #funny

== sticky-panel
topic: work
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: Want a secret? The Deck 5 panel that sticks. You lift and push. Not push and lift.
them: Calder doesn't know. She definitely knows. She knows everything. Lift and push, though.   #funny
ask: What's the best trick anyone's taught you aboard?
listen: Who taught you all this?
  them: Nobody. An old manual and a lot of getting it wrong. Mostly the getting it wrong.
share: Check the board before breakfast.
  them: Smart. I check it after breakfast. Second breakfast, sometimes.   #funny
cheer: Where the grab shelf is.
  them: The most important room on the ship. Well. Shelf. You get it.   #funny

== sleep
topic: day
when: tier>=colleague
them: I can sleep anywhere. Parts store. Tea corner. Standing up in the lift, once.
them: Except my bunk. At night. Rina says it's a medical mystery. She's writing it down.   #funny
ask: Be honest. How much are you actually sleeping?
listen: Do you really talk in your sleep?
  them: About engines, apparently. Rina says I once told a pump it was "doing great".   #funny
share: Not enough. The days are full.
  them: Same. Grab a nap at tea. Nobody minds. I've checked. Extensively.   #funny
cheer: Loads. I'm a champion sleeper.
  them: Teach me! I'll give you a screw. A good one. Not the bent one.   #funny

== mum-shop
topic: home
when: tier>=friend
them: My mum's got a little mending shop back home. Kettles, radios, coats. Anything.
them: There's a scrapyard out back. Found my first engine manual there. And a dog, mostly ears.   #warm
ask: Who taught you the stuff that really stuck?
listen: What was it like, growing up in a shop?
  them: Loud. Everything ticking. One radio that only gets one station. I miss the station.   #warm
share: My family. Little things, every day.
  them: That's how it sticks. Little things, every day. Same as here.   #warm
cheer: Trial and error. Mostly error.
  them: Ha! Best teacher going. Bit rough. Very thorough.   #funny
